{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"disgusted-fretful-hare","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe eval harnesses must work for a client project that supplies its own criteria (`.rebar/criteria_routing.json`) and corpus, using the same mechanism rebar uses for its own evals (operator ruling 2026-09-06). Today `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py:20-21` hard-codes `_DEFAULT_CACHE_DIR` and `_DEFAULT_OUT_DIR` as CWD-relative `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay[/cache]`; `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/ledger.py:43` `DEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH` is a `str` default on `reserve`, `finalize`, `charge_estimate`, `reconcile`, and `print_summary` (`:89,153,185,222,244`) and is re-exported into `tier1.py:390` and `tier2.py:561,684`, with no `--ledger` flag. A client running `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay` writes into its own `docs/experiments/`. `src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py:156` globs only packaged specs and `--out` (`:586`) defaults to the packaged results file (`:118,:491`), so a client would write into site-packages. `ledger.py:120` imports `genai_prices` bare although `evals` is a pyproject extra (`pyproject.toml:165-167`) absent from `src/rebar/_optional.py::EXTRAS` (`:35-68`). `AGENTIC_SOLVERS` (`provider_parity.py:88`) still names `\"ticket-quality\"`, which the LLM-leftovers epic retires. Cites are on origin/main 2e81cb9767c1.\n\n## Approach\nOne resolution rule: `[llm.evals] corpus_root`, read from the reserved `llm` table like `[llm.model_classes]` through `rebar.llm.config_readers._read_llm_file_table` (`src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py:37-63`); default `.rebar/evals`; this repo sets `corpus_root = \"docs/experiments\"` in `rebar.toml` for now (a sibling story flips it to `evals` when the corpus moves); env `REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT`; CLI `rebar -c llm.evals.corpus_root=...`; precedence CLI over env over file over default exactly as `_llm_str_source` (`config_readers.py:66-84`). Relative values resolve against the repo root; harness sub-paths are fixed under it: `<corpus_root>/plan-review-gate/replay/{cache/, ledger.jsonl, tier2-sample.json, <reports>.md}` and `<corpus_root>/provider-parity/provider_parity_results.json`. With `corpus_root = \"docs/experiments\"` every current literal is reproduced byte-for-byte, so this story lands with zero behaviour change. Choosing the `llm` reserved table rather than a core `_config_schema.py` section keeps this epic out of the config epic's files; the mechanism ratchet censuses core `_SECTIONS` only (`scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py:18-22,37`), so the only new mechanism is the env var, justified at its read site.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py`: add\n```python\nDEFAULT_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT = \".rebar/evals\"\ndef evals_corpus_root(repo_root=None) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"[llm.evals].corpus_root: CLI > REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT > file > default;\n    relative paths resolve against the repo root.\"\"\"\n    root = Path(str(_root_config.repo_root(repo_root)))\n    table = _read_llm_file_table(repo_root)\n    flat = {\"evals.corpus_root\": (table.get(\"evals\") or {}).get(\"corpus_root\")}\n    cli = _root_config.cli_overrides_for(\"llm\")\n    # mechanism-ok: env_var REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT — eval corpus root override for client projects\n    value = _llm_str(flat, cli, \"REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT\", \"evals.corpus_root\", DEFAULT_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT)\n    return (root / value).resolve() if not Path(value).is_absolute() else Path(value)\n```\n  plus `replay_dir(repo_root=None) -> Path` (`evals_corpus_root() / \"plan-review-gate\" / \"replay\"`) and `default_ledger_path(repo_root=None) -> str` (`replay_dir() / \"ledger.jsonl\"`). Re-export from `rebar.llm.config` in its re-export block. `-c llm.evals.corpus_root=` works because `set_cli_overrides` splits on the first dot (`src/rebar/config.py:309`).\n- `plan_replay/__main__.py`: delete `:20-21`; `--cache-dir`, `--out-dir`, `--sample-path` defaults (`:54-55,72-73,86,96-97`) become `None` and resolve at dispatch to `replay_dir()/\"cache\"`, `replay_dir()`, `replay_dir()/\"tier2-sample.json\"`; add `--ledger` (default `None`, resolving to `default_ledger_path()`) threaded into the `tier1.run` and `tier2.run_*` calls.\n- `ledger.py`: delete `DEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH`; the five `ledger_path: str = DEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH` defaults become `str | None = None` with `ledger_path = ledger_path or default_ledger_path()` as the first line; `tier1.py:390`, `tier2.py:561,684` likewise. `ledger.py:120` becomes `genai_prices = guard_import(\"genai_prices\", extra=\"evals\")`.\n- `src/rebar/_optional.py` `EXTRAS`: add `\"evals\": (\"genai_prices\", \"the plan-review replay ledger's spend accounting (python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay)\")` (`pricing` shares the probe; the `grounding`/`grounding-t2` pair is the precedent).\n- `provider_parity.py`: `:88` becomes `frozenset({\"completion-verifier\", \"spec-alignment\"})`; `:156` unions `files(\"rebar.llm\")/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml` with `<repo_root>/.rebar/evals/*.eval.yaml`, project file winning by prompt id (mirrors `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:71-75`); `--out` default `None` resolves to `evals_corpus_root()/\"provider-parity\"/\"provider_parity_results.json\"`; the packaged baseline `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json` is refreshed only by passing `--out` explicitly.\n- `rebar.toml`: add `[llm.evals]` with `corpus_root = \"docs/experiments\"`.\n- `docs/env-vars.md` regenerated (`_llm_str` is a `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` helper, `docs/env-vars.md:8`).\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py`, `src/rebar/llm/config.py` (re-export lines only), `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/{__main__,ledger,tier1,tier2}.py`, `src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py`, `src/rebar/_optional.py`, `rebar.toml`, `docs/env-vars.md`, `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py` (new), `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_ledger.py` and `tests/unit/test_provider_parity*.py` (default-path assertions), `tests/unit/test_optional.py` (the blurb loop already covers the new entry). Not touched: `src/rebar/_config_schema.py`, `src/rebar/_config_sources.py` (config epic), `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py` (LLM-leftovers epic), `src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_mining/heal.py` (already `.rebar/`-relative, `heal.py:168-173,420-462`).\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `pytest tests/unit/evals -q`; in a temp client repo after `rebar init` with no config, `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current` creates `.rebar/evals/plan-review-gate/replay/{cache,ledger.jsonl}`; in this repo a unit test asserts `evals_corpus_root() == REPO / \"docs/experiments\"`. Edge: `REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT=/tmp/x` wins over the file; `rebar -c llm.evals.corpus_root=y` wins over env; an absolute value is returned unchanged; with `genai_prices` blocked, `ledger.finalize` raises `OptionalDependencyError` naming `nava-rebar[evals]`; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` and `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` are green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -n 'docs/experiments' -- src/rebar/llm/evals` returns only docstring cites (`corpus.py:5`, `legacy_v4_baseline.py:2-6`), asserted by `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py::test_no_hard_coded_roots`.\n- [ ] Default, env, CLI, and file precedence are proven by four parametrised cases in the new test module.\n- [ ] `python -c \"from rebar._optional import EXTRAS; print('evals' in EXTRAS)\"` prints `True` and the ledger degrades with an `OptionalDependencyError` naming the extra.\n- [ ] `python -c \"from rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity import AGENTIC_SOLVERS; print(sorted(AGENTIC_SOLVERS))\"` prints `['completion-verifier', 'spec-alignment']`.\n- [ ] Rebar's own replay outputs are path-identical before and after (`corpus_root = \"docs/experiments\"` pinned; `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py` unchanged and green).\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"d279-4cf9-d1a6-4f7b","parent_id":"e47b-d3ef-338f-4bcd","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"One configured corpus root for plan-replay, ledger, and provider-parity; register the evals extra"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788805645824287142,"uuid":"1fc62c85-12b2-433a-b93a-c37d33d116f6"}